charlie_customer: Hey team — our integration started failing during a tool call. We only see this when the tool_args contain inline comments or a multiline config block. API returns 400 with: "invalid JSON in tool_args (unexpected token)". request_id=req_9f3b2a. Any ideas? :confused:

sophie_support: Sorry about that — can you drop a minimal repro (curl or curl-like) and the request_id? I can try to reproduce. Also pinging @ryan_oncall if this looks like a runtime change. :eyes:

charlie_customer: Minimal repro below (sanitized):
```bash
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -H 'Authorization: Bearer xxxxx' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{
  "model": "tool-runner-1",
  "input": "invoke-tool",
  "tool_call": {
    "name": "config_apply",
    "tool_args": {
      // developer note: keep legacy field for backward compat
      /* multiline comment: this is generated from a template */
      "env": "prod",
      "flags": [
        "fast",
        "safe"
      ]
    }
  }
}'
```
This fails immediately. If I remove the // or /* */ comments it works.

sophie_support: Reproduced locally with your payload. Here's the parser error from our logs: "tool_args: invalid JSON at offset 94 (unexpected //)". Sentry link: https://sentry.redwood.ai/issue/RED-8721 (internal). Looks like our runtime is using a strict JSON parser that rejects comments.

charlie_customer: We generate config templates with comments (JSON5 style) — converting on client is non-trivial across our stack. Any temporary workaround other than stripping comments server-side? Base64 encoding the whole tool_args body and decoding in the tool would be awful for observability.

sophie_support: Understood. I'm escalating. @ryan_oncall tagging runtime for visibility. I've created ENG-4721 and attached your repro.

ryan_oncall: Confirmed — runtime 2.14 switched to strict JSON parsing to avoid ambiguous inputs; we didn't add a helpful validation message, so clients see a 400 generic error. Short term we should: 1) return 422 with a clear message when comments are detected, 2) surface guidance in support docs. Long term we can consider opt-in JSON5 parsing but that has security/consistency implications. Can you add a tiny repro file to ENG-4721 so we can add a regression?

lee_runtime: I'll prepare a tight fix to improve the error string and run a quick validation pass before the handler to catch comment tokens earlier. Plan: update validator to detect comment tokens and respond with 422 + "tool_args contains comments; remove comments or provide pure JSON". I'll add a unit test with your curl. ETA a few hours. deploy-bot: please queue staging deploy when ready. :thumbsup:

deploy-bot: staging-deploy/2024-05-27-1719 queued by lee_runtime — monitor: https://deploys.redwood.ai/staging/1139

sophie_support: In the meantime, a small client-side quickfix you can run as a stopgap (node):
```js
// strip-comments.js - naive removal of // and /* */ comments
const fs = require('fs');
let s = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8'); // read stdin
s = s.replace(/\/\/.*$/gm, '');
s = s.replace(/\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\//g, '');
console.log(s);
```
Pipe your payload through this before sending. Not ideal but works while we patch.

charlie_customer: Thanks — I'll try the script. Please cc me on ENG-4721 updates. Also would love to avoid base64 since it breaks observability.

ryan_oncall: Will ping you once the staging validation change is merged and tested. Assigning ENG-4721 -> runtime-team. ETA for staging merge: ~3 hours, prod rollout pending smoke tests.

lee_runtime: Merged a tiny validator change to the staging branch and added the regression test. Will follow up with a changelog blurb.

sophie_support: Thanks everyone — charlie_customer, I'll DM you the Sentry link and add you to ENG-4721 watchers so you're notified. Apologies for the disruption. :pray:

charlie_customer: Appreciate the quick turnaround.
